  "equipment_type": "Process loop controller via BACnet gateway",
  "applies_to": "Honeywell UDC 2500 loop controllers supplied on Cleaver-Brooks equipment, read through a ProtoNode RER gateway.",
  "summary": "The ProtoNode maps the UDC 2500 controller to BACnet: process variable, remote variable, inputs, alarm states and actions as AIs, and working setpoint, output, tuning, alarm setpoints, limits, overrides, local/remote setpoint and auto/manual selection as writable AVs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50000 + Modbus Node-ID",
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Each Cleaver-Brooks controller on the ProtoNode is its own BACnet device; the object instances below are the same on every device.",
    "The guide prints no write-point stars for this profile; the AV/BV objects map to Metasys N2 outputs and Modbus output registers or coils, so they are taken as writable. Access is inferred from object type.",
    "The guide gives no engineering units or state texts; units appear only where the object name carries them (DEG F / DEG C).",
    "Where a description is filled in, it gives the register from the guide's Modbus column."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Cloud Enabled ProtoNode Gateway Startup Guide (RER/LER) for interfacing Cleaver-Brooks products",
    "doc_number": "750-426",
    "revision_date": "03/2018",
    "url": "https://watmfg.com/watmfg23082016/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/750-426-ProtoNode-Cloud.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "host": "watmfg.com"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read the process variable and output; write the local setpoint and auto/manual mode only if the BMS is meant to adjust the loop.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 14",
        "why": "Local setpoint 1",
        "name": "SP1_LSP1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 30",
        "why": "Auto/manual selection",
        "name": "AutoMan"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "why": "Process variable",
        "name": "PV"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "why": "Working setpoint",
        "name": "WorkingSP"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "why": "Controller output",
        "name": "Output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10",
        "why": "Alarm status bits 1-16",
        "name": "AlarmStat1_16"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet Device Instance = the controller's Modbus Node-ID + Node_Offset (default 50,000), so Node-ID 1 = 50001. Change Node_Offset in the ProtoNode web configurator to pick other instances.",
      "The ProtoNode RER does BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP, selected on its S bank DIP switches.",
      "BACnet MS/TP: one MAC address (1-127) for the whole ProtoNode on the A bank DIP switches; baud on B0-B3 (38400 factory default).",
      "BACnet IP: default ProtoNode address 192.168.1.24; change it in the web configurator."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Tuning (gain, reset, rate) and limit AVs change the controller's configuration; don't write them cyclically."
    ]
  },
